near-death experiences hypothermia and  an icebreaker no one saw coming oh and  then there was the time the whole crew  was drugged  one of the most bizarre things to happen  on the Titanic set happened while  filming the framing narrative centered  around Bill Paxton's character Brock  Lovett and his search of the wreck of  the Titanic Marilyn McAvoy a background  painter who worked on Titanic spoke to  Vice about the incident which occurred  in 1996 when some cast and Crews sat  down to enjoy a clam chowder lunch there  was only one problem it was spiked with  PCP those affected including James  Cameron and actor Bill Paxton were  rushed to the hospital both Kate Winslet  and Leonardo DiCaprio were spared to  this eventful dinner since they weren't  required for this Canadian shoot he said  what did you eat the clam chowder and I  thought well yeah I had a couple of  bowls and about that time I started  feeling it Marilyn McAvoy recalls how  the evening began with people going for  seconds and thirds of the Chowder  because it tasted so good everyone was  having a lot more than they usually  would soon people started tripping and  once they realized what was happening  Cameron allegedly went up to his room to  make himself throw up and stop the  hallucinogen from taking over McAvoy  described how the crew was in the  hospital all night as some people were  having a bad trip she said it became  pretty chaotic people had a lot of  energy some were in wheelchairs flying  down the hallways people were playing  hacky sack Bill Paxton also opened up to  Larry King about the incident describing  the hospital scene that night in much  the same way you see some people are  freaking out some people are Congo  dancing some people are euphoric I I  knew I was pretty Stoned on her end  McAvoy said it all seemed like a dream  and that her experience wasn't too bad  unfortunately for the crew they never  caught the perpetrator resulting in that  entire night going down as one of the  weirdest onset moments once the Titanic  sinks Jack freezes in The Frigid Waters  but Rose manages to stay alive and flag  down a nearby boat looking for survivors  it's a tragic ending but Rose's  shivering tears weren't pure acting it  was cold as hell in that water in 2017  Kate Winslet appeared on The Late Show  with Stephen Colbert and revealed that  when shooting this scene in the water  she got hypothermia yeah I  she further explained that even though  this was all supposed to be pretend  movie Magic there was so much water that  the crew couldn't heat it all up hey  maybe if DiCaprio had just climbed up on  that piece of wood to keep her warm nah  never mind there's no way there was room  for him no possible way  it turns out Kate Winslet suffered quite  a bit during filming in a 1997 interview  with the Los Angeles Times Winslet  revealed a variety of injuries she got  on set bruises gashes and a chipped  elbow she also described the moment when  she almost drowned during one scene what  makes this even more bizarre is the fact  that Cameron didn't notice and kept  directing as he was completely oblivious  to her near-death experience the scene  in question takes place when Rose and  Jack are running through the ship as  water is gushing in they tried to find  an Escape Route but soon get trapped in  by a closed gate with water pouring in  on them once the scene was cut the  production team opened the gate to allow  DiCaprio and Winslet through however her  coat got caught on the iron bars and she  was submerged in the water wenzlit  described the experience to the Los  Angeles Times saying I had no breath  left I thought I'd burst and Jim just  said okay let's go again that was his  attitude I didn't want to be a wimp so I  didn't complain well I'm fine  I'll be fine  really although Cameron realized a few  minutes later that Winslet was feeling  shaken by The Experience he wanted to  get back into it and shoot the scene  again comparing it to getting back on a  horse after a fall The Show Must Go On  after all  for many the staircase in Titanic is an  iconic symbol of rose and Jack's love  early in the film Jack waits for Rose at  the bottom of the staircase to escort  her to dinner with her family he's blown  away when he sees her looking fancy and  beautiful and the Romantic tension  between them is palpable in the final  scene of the movie Rose passes away and  the staircase appears again reuniting  her with Jack and all of the others lost  on the Titanic both are beautiful and  emotional moments as they show the  Journey of Jack and Rose's relationship  culminating with their final Embrace in  the afterlife however behind the scenes  of this romantic tale is a puzzling  story in 2017 Cameron reflected on his  time filming Titanic in National  Geographic's Titanic 20 years later with  James Cameron when looking back at the  iconic staircase Cameron recalled the  staircase has got a steel footing then  when we sank the ship it lifted wood is  buoyant it ripped off that footing and  it all floated up and it actually pinned  two stunt players fortunately they  weren't hurt but it was a pretty scary  moment the staircase was built to  replicate the actual Grand stairs that  were award the famous vessel so perhaps  it brought some of its bad luck with it  Brett Baker Leonardo DiCaprio's photo  double in Titanic spoke to Vanity Fair  in 2016 about his experience making the  film Baker was a struggling actor and  was thrilled to join the project even  though the role wasn't exactly what he  trained for as a photo double Baker's  job was to silently take DiCaprio's  place in shots where you couldn't see  his face to give the star a break from  more tedious work Baker's presence in  Titanic is undetectable but he remembers  how nervous he was to meet Cameron for  the first time since he is both shorter  and older than DiCaprio luckily Cameron  believed he looked enough like DiCaprio  that it would work Baker looks back  fondly on his time on the Titanic set  saying most actors don't get their big  breaks starring in one of the biggest  films of all time plus the photo double  life got interesting thanks to all of  the Teen fans waiting by the studio gate  hoping to catch a glimpse of DiCaprio  during the filming of Titanic the Leo  craze was in full swing security would  Usher DiCaprio out the back to avoid the  fans and Baker would be brought out  front for everyone to gush over turning  him into a real-life photo double for  the star as Baker recalls to Vanity Fair  the fans went berserk screaming looking  inside the window waving their pieces of  paper for an autograph I don't know if  anyone knew that was going on at the  gate every morning at least he got his  own little fan club during filming  actors have been known to take things  from set from time to time think of it  less as stealing and more is holding  onto a piece of memorabilia that  commemorates the time they spent filming  it's understandable when one goes  through Blood Sweat and Tears to make a  film that they feel like they deserve a  little something for their troubles  aside from their massive paycheck of  course when slit did almost drown and  get hypothermia maybe it's fair to say  that she wanted to take a little  something extra on the way out in an  interview with the New York Times she  revealed that she likes saving things  from sets and during Titanic she snagged  some jewelry she explained I did take a  pair of rose's earrings but somewhere I  lost one it's a fitting story since  Titanic itself is framed around a search  for lost jewelry a necklace that of  course gets lost in the ocean at the end  it's no secret that Leonardo Dicaprio  and Kate Winslet have enjoyed a  decades-long friendship ever since  starring a star-crossed lovers in  Titanic the two have freely shown each  other their admiration and support over  the years a decade after Titanic the two  starred in the post-war romantic drama  Revolutionary Road Winslet talked about  her friendship with DiCaprio in an  interview with the guardian noting that  they've known each other for half their  lives she said he's my friend my really  close friend we're bonded for Life  when's lit won the Golden Globe for best  actress in 2009 for Revolutionary Road  and gushed about her co-star in Her  off-the-cuff speech for his part  DiCaprio has described how Winslet broke  the ice between the two right off the  bat and the official behind the scenes  book of the film at w Marsh's James  Cameron's Titanic DiCaprio shared their  bizarre first encounter that did just  that the first scene he shot was the one  where he draws naked Rose DiCaprio  explained Winslet had no shame with it  she wanted to break the ice a little  beforehand so she flashed me I wasn't  prepared for that so she had one up on  me I was pretty comfortable after that a  1998 Rolling Stone profile on Winslet  detailed how things snowballed from  there with Winslet and DiCaprio spending  the rest of the shoot pranking each  other and forming a very comfortable  relationship Winslet explained we were  kind of the two goofy kids on the set we  do the most ridiculous things to each  other he be tickling me groping me  winding me up and I'd be doing the same  thing back sort of grabbing his bum  Caprio discussed the seriousness of  their friendship on set as well saying  she was my best friend for seven months  we'd unload the stresses of the shoot to  each other vent to each other watch out  for each other Kate was just the perfect  person to work with because she was very  much one of the guys and it would have  been much harder without her we were  Partners  oh that was better you got to work on it  really try and honk it up and get some  body to it you know you gotta  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]
 

